  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The spin – fake, turn and one-timer",
  "description": "Two lines at the centre line. The first in line A dribbles towards the goal, fakes a shot on the goalkeeper and carries on around a cone (the spin). Coming out, A looks up and passes to the first in line B, who has timed their run through a gate of two cones so the pass reaches the blade right there. B finishes with a one-timer.\n\nThe players swap lines behind the goal. The drill uses half the court. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Make the shot fake convincing – the goalkeeper has to buy it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up as you come out of the spin, before you pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B: adjust your speed so you are in the gate when the pass arrives."
    }
  ],
